    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change extends the existing `toBusinessDay` roll-forward loop in the most natural way possible: it adds a single `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(adjusted)` clause to the same `while` condition that already handles Saturday/Sunday. The logic stays in the one unit that already owns business-day adjustment, so there is no new method, no duplicated roll logic, and no second place a future maintainer would have to keep in sync.\n\nThe holiday list is a well-named `static final Set<LocalDate>` sitting alongside the other domain constants in the class (e.g. `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`), consistent with how this class already holds its tuning values. Placing it in the controller matches the existing convention \u2014 the weekend-rolling logic already lives here, so co-locating the holiday set is coherent rather than scattering related rules.\n\nThe Javadoc was updated accurately to describe the new one-day-at-a-time roll and the non-holiday-weekday termination condition, keeping the documentation in step with the code. Nothing is becoming a catch-all here; this is a focused, additive extension of an existing responsibility.",
